{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-parity-regime-selection","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:parity-regime-selection","kind":"proof","title":"Proof of parity regime selection","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-parity-regime-selection"],"text":"parity-regime-selection-proof.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prf:parity-regime-selection\"></a><p>Write <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a = -a'</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b = -b'</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a', b' > 0</code>, and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">N = M + 1</code>. Then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A - 1 = Z + M</code> and</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  (-1)^{Z+M}\\, a^Z\\, b^{M} = (-1)^{Z+M}(-1)^{Z}(-1)^{M}\\, a'^Z\\, b'^M = a'^Z\\, b'^M > 0,</code></pre>\n<p>since <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(-1)^{2(Z+M)} = 1</code>. <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\square</code></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/parity-regime-selection-proof.md","heading":"Proof","page":"b/prf-parity-regime-selection","qa":{"counts":{"pass":54,"fail":2,"warn":0,"na":18,"unknown":0,"stale":58},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
